{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UL9uUNMhYZQqpaxNRvqF9K","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c21a7cbfa2c9f67c1991372a343217e949e04f44\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T18:15:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6683: Skip full-text search with drugs when a concept is provided (#6346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"375abbe5b5f9a52df6ea4cce33fc3ecdfba16c77\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T16:35:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6516: Follow-up: fix tests\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"11489bdb02063ff8138f45803c336b7ef4635179\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T08:26:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6687: Improve performance of searches using the search index (#6342)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eb0a1006c7e188d4408deb298685c98ea1fef321\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T07:59:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6688: Fix circular initialization error in logging setup (#6341)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d8fe1365fbce0b4d3fc43045dff3b69ce58ca2f4\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T16:25:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"Require privileges for unprotected CohortService methods (#6317)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Require Purge Cohorts privilege for CohortService.purgeCohort\\n\\npurgeCohort permanently and irreversibly removes a cohort from the\\ndatabase but carried no @Authorized annotation, so any authenticated\\nuser could reach it through the REST purge path\\n(DELETE /ws/rest/v1/cohort/{uuid}?purge=true), even though the\\nreversible voidCohort on the same resource requires Delete Cohorts.\\nA dedicated Purge Cohorts privilege already exists in PrivilegeConstants\\nbut was never applied. Annotate purgeCohort with it, consistent with the\\nrest of the service.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for Purge Cohorts authorization\\n\\nGuards the @Authorized gate on CohortService.purgeCohort so that\\ndropping the annotation fails the build instead of silently\\nreopening the purge path to unprivileged callers.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Require Get Patient Cohorts privilege for CohortService.getCohorts\\n\\ngetCohorts(String) was the only read on the service with no\\n@Authorized, reading straight from the DAO while every sibling\\ngetter requires Get Patient Cohorts. A direct service-layer caller\\ncould therefore list cohorts (names, descriptions, member patient\\nids) with no authorization; the REST search path was only covered\\nincidentally by the resource's required-get privilege at conversion\\ntime. Gate it at the service layer to match the other getters.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Assert the specific privilege in cohort authorization tests\\n\\nCapture the thrown APIAuthenticationException and assert its message\\nnames the required privilege, so a future edit that swaps either\\nannotation to a different privilege (for purgeCohort, the exact\\nregression this PR fixes: gating on Get Patient Cohorts instead of\\nPurge Cohorts) fails the build rather than staying green.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Use containsString matcher for cohort authorization assertions\\n\\nassertThat(msg, containsString(privilege)) reports the actual message\\non failure, so a future privilege regression is self-describing in the\\nCI log instead of the bare \\\"expected true but was false\\\" that\\nassertTrue(msg.contains(..)) produces.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9c515246b4f37eafec0d6fc24de5b0455b9e3951\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T02:38:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"mergePatients does not reassign Conditions, Allergies, or MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient (#6198) (#6315)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* mergePatients now reassigns Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient\\n\\nPatientServiceImpl.mergePatients had no reassignment helpers for the\\npatient-scoped Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses tables, which\\nwere added to core after the merge logic was written. After a merge these\\nclinical records stayed attached to the now-voided non-preferred patient and\\nsilently disappeared from the surviving patient's record - a clinical-data-loss\\nand patient-safety concern (e.g. a hidden allergy).\\n\\nAdd mergeConditions, mergeAllergies and mergeMedicationDispenses helpers that\\nmove each non-voided record from the non-preferred to the preferred patient via\\nthe corresponding services, mirroring the existing\\nmergeObservationsNotContainedInEncounters pattern. Saving through the services\\nkeeps the changes audited and emits the normal save events. The moves are\\nrecorded in new PersonMergeLogData collections so they appear in the\\nPersonMergeLog.\\n\\nAllergies are deduplicated by allergen: an allergy whose allergen the preferred\\npatient already records is not moved, because a patient cannot hold two\\nallergies for the same allergen and a duplicate would make the survivor's\\nallergy list fail to load afterwards.\\n\\nFixes #6194\\n\\n\\n\\n* Keep @since on the new PersonMergeLogData accessors only, not the private fields\\n\\nThe moved* fields are private (not API and not rendered by Javadoc), so the\\nfield-level @since 2.9.0 tags were redundant. The public getters/adders keep\\n@since 2.9.0, matching the codebase convention (Patient, Condition, Allergy\\nattach @since to accessors, not backing fields).\\n\\n\\n\\n---------\\n\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 51422097a51a0918a9524ce8c0bd3aa76d17e25a)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a2d22b85955401c2d12d3ebecd9e3f483cd905e8\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T01:34:15+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6675: Module is not updated when omod changes (#6257) (#6314)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6675: Module is not updated when omod changes\\n\\n* TRUNK-6675: Address review comments\\n\\n- Split the deleteDirectory try-catch in the optimized-startup branch so IOException from deletion logs an accurate message instead of \\\"Error while reading module last modified file\\\"\\n- Pin getLibCacheFolderForModule_shouldRecreateNonEmptyDirWhenModuleChanged to the module-changed branch by explicitly setting optimized.startup=true\\n\\n\\n\\n* TRUNK-6675: Address review comments\\n\\n- Extract deleteLibCacheDir helper to reduce cognitive complexity (fixes SonarCloud quality gate)\\n- Guard .moduleLastModified write on successful deletion so a failed delete does not mask the problem on the next restart\\n- Fix Context.getRuntimeProperties() defensive-copy bug in both tests: mutate the copy and push it back via Context.setRuntimeProperties() so isOptimizedStartup() actually sees the change\\n\\n\\n\\n* Update api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/ModuleClassLoader.java\\n\\n\\n\\n---------\\n\\n\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 918f05117302df56e7fb74193ffd4e4cf926d0ed)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Rafal Korytkowski <rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\\n\\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\\n\\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\\n\\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\\n\\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\\n\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\\n\\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\\n\\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\\n  picked up without any module-side call\\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"17c7d2c4111bc928fd3d7bb90f6d767903ef032a\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T23:26:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"Revert \\\"Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes (#6305)\\\" (#6312)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This reverts commit 4abaae2eebcf54375d5304d95a18c4b1e0a44cf7.\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9533e285323873ae4ace289f2dfee0cd931d5622\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T23:05:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"Clean up the module jar copy in ModuleClassLoader (#6307)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The module jar copy in getModuleUrls() managed its streams by hand and\\nclosed them in a finally block that calls close() on references that are\\nstill null when opening the input stream throws, relying on the\\nsurrounding catch to swallow the resulting NullPointerException. Replace\\nit with try-with-resources, which closes both streams in reverse order\\nwith proper suppressed-exception handling and only closes the ones that\\nwere actually opened.\\n\\nAlso drop the preceding \\\"if (!tmpModuleJar.exists()) createNewFile()\\\"\\nblock: the FileOutputStream that copies into it creates the file anyway,\\nso the pre-creation is redundant.\\n\\nBehaviour is unchanged; an IOException while copying is still caught and\\nlogged.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4abaae2eebcf54375d5304d95a18c4b1e0a44cf7\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T23:04:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes (#6305)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes\\n\\nModuleClassLoader.getLibCacheFolderForModule() wipes a module's lib cache\\nfolder when the module file changed (or on non-optimized startup) so the\\nmodule is fully re-expanded. It used File.delete(), which only removes an\\nempty directory and silently no-ops on a populated one, and the return\\nvalue was ignored. The cache folder always holds the module jar,\\nlib/*.jar and the .moduleLastModified marker, so the delete never\\nhappened.\\n\\nAs a result, any jar a module dropped between versions stayed in the\\ncache and on the module classpath after an in-place upgrade, causing\\nstale classes and version or class-identity conflicts that are hard to\\ndiagnose because the omod on disk looks correct. Fresh installs are\\nunaffected.\\n\\nReplace both delete sites with a recursive FileUtils.deleteDirectory()\\nhelper, and harden the surrounding logic so a stale classpath cannot slip\\nthrough silently:\\n\\n- If the .moduleLastModified marker cannot be read or parsed, we can no\\n  longer tell whether the module changed, so clear the cache rather than\\n  reuse it.\\n- If the folder still cannot be fully cleared (for example a jar locked\\n  by the OS during a hot reload), warn with an actionable message instead\\n  of quietly expanding over the stale content.\\n- Check the mkdirs() result so a cache folder that cannot be recreated is\\n  visible rather than surfacing later as an obscure expansion failure.\\n- Guard the recursive delete to a direct child of the lib cache root so a\\n  malformed module id can never point it outside the cache.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Retry the lib cache prune on the next startup when it cannot complete\\n\\nTwo hardening changes to the recursive delete, from review:\\n\\n- getLibCacheFolderForModule no longer refreshes the .moduleLastModified\\n  marker when the folder could not be fully cleared (e.g. jars still\\n  locked by the previous classloader during a hot upgrade on Windows).\\n  Stamping the new value over leftovers made every later optimized\\n  startup trust the stale cache, so jars the delete failed to remove\\n  would have stayed on the module classpath indefinitely; with a stale\\n  or missing marker the next startup retries the delete once the locks\\n  are gone and self-heals.\\n\\n- A stray regular file sitting at the cache folder's path is deleted\\n  explicitly: FileUtils.deleteDirectory throws an unchecked\\n  IllegalArgumentException for a non-directory, which would escape the\\n  IOException catch and fail the module's startup, where the previous\\n  File#delete() silently recovered.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Harden the lib cache prune: pin the marker refresh and polish\\n\\n- Assert in the prune test that a successful clear refreshes the\\n  .moduleLastModified marker; without this a regression that skipped\\n  every marker write would pass the suite while silently turning each\\n  optimized startup into a full cache wipe and re-expansion.\\n- Rename the unreadable-marker test to \\\"unparseable\\\": it exercises the\\n  NumberFormatException arm of the catch, not the IOException arm.\\n- Extract a moduleWithTempOmod test helper for the repeated\\n  module-plus-temp-omod fixture.\\n- Document in deleteLibCacheFolder why a disposed classloader keeps\\n  working on POSIX after the prune (unlink preserves its open jar\\n  handles, unlike the previous in-place overwrite that corrupted them)\\n  and that the guard refusal also returns false.\\n- Align the marker read/write warning wording.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e72a818d09b603a075ddf1040be58c9291ddb47b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-08T21:31:54+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6674: List backport releases in the minutes code @since tag (#6269)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The constant landed on 2.8.x and 2.9.x after the backports merged, so\\nthe tag now lists 2.8.8, 2.9.0 and 3.0.0 in the style of the existing\\nmulti-release tags in OpenmrsConstants. The other constants introduced\\nby TRUNK-6674 remain 3.0.0 only, since the UCUM resolution was\\ndeliberately not backported.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4d8d419630e1ff1d46616c38573f429fd3038ff8\",\"date\":\"2026-07-08T20:47:03+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6674: Resolve drug order duration units across all known SNOMED CT and UCUM codes (#6246)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Saving a drug order whose duration units concept carries the current\\nSNOMED CT minute code 1156209001 failed with HTTP 500. SNOMED CT\\ninactivated the legacy minute code 258701004 in its 2021-07-31 release\\nand dictionaries such as CIEL now map Minutes to the active code.\\n\\nResolve duration units deterministically from all of a concept's\\nSAME-AS mappings via Duration.getDuration(Integer, Concept): SNOMED CT\\nmappings take priority and UCUM strictly fills gaps, unresolvable units\\nfail at validation instead of at save time, and getCode is deprecated\\nwith behavior unchanged. The vocabulary registries are compiled in by\\ndesign; the class Javadoc records the invariants and TRUNK-6674 records\\nthe alternatives considered.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00\",\"message\":\"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"rkorytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a6ec6555bcd71f00d07a25d2f2e8f089c4842451\",\"date\":\"2026-06-30T11:29:11+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6515: Include message broker for publishing / subscribing to external events (#6205)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit bda3963b815c36dcd768d9e515024eaff7f482a4)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":73}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00eccacc-1e98-4eb4-96ca-fdcfe7265154","uuid":"5f244026-9eac-4e3b-9984-ed9915dadf30","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:06:04.521Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"c21a7cbfa2c9f67c1991372a343217e949e04f44\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T18:15:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6683: Skip full-text search with drugs when a concept is provided (#6346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"375abbe5b5f9a52df6ea4cce33fc3ecdfba16c77\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T16:35:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6516: Follow-up: fix tests\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"11489bdb02063ff8138f45803c336b7ef4635179\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T08:26:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6687: Improve performance of searches using the search index (#6342)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"eb0a1006c7e188d4408deb298685c98ea1fef321\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T07:59:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6688: Fix circular initialization error in logging setup (#6341)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d8fe1365fbce0b4d3fc43045dff3b69ce58ca2f4\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T16:25:59+03:00\",\"message\":\"Require privileges for unprotected CohortService methods (#6317)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Require Purge Cohorts privilege for CohortService.purgeCohort\\n\\npurgeCohort permanently and irreversibly removes a cohort from the\\ndatabase but carried no @Authorized annotation, so any authenticated\\nuser could reach it through the REST purge path\\n(DELETE /ws/rest/v1/cohort/{uuid}?purge=true), even though the\\nreversible voidCohort on the same resource requires Delete Cohorts.\\nA dedicated Purge Cohorts privilege already exists in PrivilegeConstants\\nbut was never applied. Annotate purgeCohort with it, consistent with the\\nrest of the service.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for Purge Cohorts authorization\\n\\nGuards the @Authorized gate on CohortService.purgeCohort so that\\ndropping the annotation fails the build instead of silently\\nreopening the purge path to unprivileged callers.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Require Get Patient Cohorts privilege for CohortService.getCohorts\\n\\ngetCohorts(String) was the only read on the service with no\\n@Authorized, reading straight from the DAO while every sibling\\ngetter requires Get Patient Cohorts. A direct service-layer caller\\ncould therefore list cohorts (names, descriptions, member patient\\nids) with no authorization; the REST search path was only covered\\nincidentally by the resource's required-get privilege at conversion\\ntime. Gate it at the service layer to match the other getters.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Assert the specific privilege in cohort authorization tests\\n\\nCapture the thrown APIAuthenticationException and assert its message\\nnames the required privilege, so a future edit that swaps either\\nannotation to a different privilege (for purgeCohort, the exact\\nregression this PR fixes: gating on Get Patient Cohorts instead of\\nPurge Cohorts) fails the build rather than staying green.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Use containsString matcher for cohort authorization assertions\\n\\nassertThat(msg, containsString(privilege)) reports the actual message\\non failure, so a future privilege regression is self-describing in the\\nCI log instead of the bare \\\"expected true but was false\\\" that\\nassertTrue(msg.contains(..)) produces.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9c515246b4f37eafec0d6fc24de5b0455b9e3951\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T02:38:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"mergePatients does not reassign Conditions, Allergies, or MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient (#6198) (#6315)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* mergePatients now reassigns Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient\\n\\nPatientServiceImpl.mergePatients had no reassignment helpers for the\\npatient-scoped Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses tables, which\\nwere added to core after the merge logic was written. After a merge these\\nclinical records stayed attached to the now-voided non-preferred patient and\\nsilently disappeared from the surviving patient's record - a clinical-data-loss\\nand patient-safety concern (e.g. a hidden allergy).\\n\\nAdd mergeConditions, mergeAllergies and mergeMedicationDispenses helpers that\\nmove each non-voided record from the non-preferred to the preferred patient via\\nthe corresponding services, mirroring the existing\\nmergeObservationsNotContainedInEncounters pattern. Saving through the services\\nkeeps the changes audited and emits the normal save events. The moves are\\nrecorded in new PersonMergeLogData collections so they appear in the\\nPersonMergeLog.\\n\\nAllergies are deduplicated by allergen: an allergy whose allergen the preferred\\npatient already records is not moved, because a patient cannot hold two\\nallergies for the same allergen and a duplicate would make the survivor's\\nallergy list fail to load afterwards.\\n\\nFixes #6194\\n\\n\\n\\n* Keep @since on the new PersonMergeLogData accessors only, not the private fields\\n\\nThe moved* fields are private (not API and not rendered by Javadoc), so the\\nfield-level @since 2.9.0 tags were redundant. The public getters/adders keep\\n@since 2.9.0, matching the codebase convention (Patient, Condition, Allergy\\nattach @since to accessors, not backing fields).\\n\\n\\n\\n---------\\n\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 51422097a51a0918a9524ce8c0bd3aa76d17e25a)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a2d22b85955401c2d12d3ebecd9e3f483cd905e8\",\"date\":\"2026-07-15T01:34:15+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6675: Module is not updated when omod changes (#6257) (#6314)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6675: Module is not updated when omod changes\\n\\n* TRUNK-6675: Address review comments\\n\\n- Split the deleteDirectory try-catch in the optimized-startup branch so IOException from deletion logs an accurate message instead of \\\"Error while reading module last modified file\\\"\\n- Pin getLibCacheFolderForModule_shouldRecreateNonEmptyDirWhenModuleChanged to the module-changed branch by explicitly setting optimized.startup=true\\n\\n\\n\\n* TRUNK-6675: Address review comments\\n\\n- Extract deleteLibCacheDir helper to reduce cognitive complexity (fixes SonarCloud quality gate)\\n- Guard .moduleLastModified write on successful deletion so a failed delete does not mask the problem on the next restart\\n- Fix Context.getRuntimeProperties() defensive-copy bug in both tests: mutate the copy and push it back via Context.setRuntimeProperties() so isOptimizedStartup() actually sees the change\\n\\n\\n\\n* Update api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/ModuleClassLoader.java\\n\\n\\n\\n---------\\n\\n\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 918f05117302df56e7fb74193ffd4e4cf926d0ed)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Rafal Korytkowski <rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\\n\\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\\n\\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\\n\\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\\n\\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\\n\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\\n\\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\\n\\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\\n  picked up without any module-side call\\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"17c7d2c4111bc928fd3d7bb90f6d767903ef032a\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T23:26:05+03:00\",\"message\":\"Revert \\\"Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes (#6305)\\\" (#6312)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"This reverts commit 4abaae2eebcf54375d5304d95a18c4b1e0a44cf7.\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9533e285323873ae4ace289f2dfee0cd931d5622\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T23:05:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"Clean up the module jar copy in ModuleClassLoader (#6307)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The module jar copy in getModuleUrls() managed its streams by hand and\\nclosed them in a finally block that calls close() on references that are\\nstill null when opening the input stream throws, relying on the\\nsurrounding catch to swallow the resulting NullPointerException. Replace\\nit with try-with-resources, which closes both streams in reverse order\\nwith proper suppressed-exception handling and only closes the ones that\\nwere actually opened.\\n\\nAlso drop the preceding \\\"if (!tmpModuleJar.exists()) createNewFile()\\\"\\nblock: the FileOutputStream that copies into it creates the file anyway,\\nso the pre-creation is redundant.\\n\\nBehaviour is unchanged; an IOException while copying is still caught and\\nlogged.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4abaae2eebcf54375d5304d95a18c4b1e0a44cf7\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T23:04:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes (#6305)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes\\n\\nModuleClassLoader.getLibCacheFolderForModule() wipes a module's lib cache\\nfolder when the module file changed (or on non-optimized startup) so the\\nmodule is fully re-expanded. It used File.delete(), which only removes an\\nempty directory and silently no-ops on a populated one, and the return\\nvalue was ignored. The cache folder always holds the module jar,\\nlib/*.jar and the .moduleLastModified marker, so the delete never\\nhappened.\\n\\nAs a result, any jar a module dropped between versions stayed in the\\ncache and on the module classpath after an in-place upgrade, causing\\nstale classes and version or class-identity conflicts that are hard to\\ndiagnose because the omod on disk looks correct. Fresh installs are\\nunaffected.\\n\\nReplace both delete sites with a recursive FileUtils.deleteDirectory()\\nhelper, and harden the surrounding logic so a stale classpath cannot slip\\nthrough silently:\\n\\n- If the .moduleLastModified marker cannot be read or parsed, we can no\\n  longer tell whether the module changed, so clear the cache rather than\\n  reuse it.\\n- If the folder still cannot be fully cleared (for example a jar locked\\n  by the OS during a hot reload), warn with an actionable message instead\\n  of quietly expanding over the stale content.\\n- Check the mkdirs() result so a cache folder that cannot be recreated is\\n  visible rather than surfacing later as an obscure expansion failure.\\n- Guard the recursive delete to a direct child of the lib cache root so a\\n  malformed module id can never point it outside the cache.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Retry the lib cache prune on the next startup when it cannot complete\\n\\nTwo hardening changes to the recursive delete, from review:\\n\\n- getLibCacheFolderForModule no longer refreshes the .moduleLastModified\\n  marker when the folder could not be fully cleared (e.g. jars still\\n  locked by the previous classloader during a hot upgrade on Windows).\\n  Stamping the new value over leftovers made every later optimized\\n  startup trust the stale cache, so jars the delete failed to remove\\n  would have stayed on the module classpath indefinitely; with a stale\\n  or missing marker the next startup retries the delete once the locks\\n  are gone and self-heals.\\n\\n- A stray regular file sitting at the cache folder's path is deleted\\n  explicitly: FileUtils.deleteDirectory throws an unchecked\\n  IllegalArgumentException for a non-directory, which would escape the\\n  IOException catch and fail the module's startup, where the previous\\n  File#delete() silently recovered.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Harden the lib cache prune: pin the marker refresh and polish\\n\\n- Assert in the prune test that a successful clear refreshes the\\n  .moduleLastModified marker; without this a regression that skipped\\n  every marker write would pass the suite while silently turning each\\n  optimized startup into a full cache wipe and re-expansion.\\n- Rename the unreadable-marker test to \\\"unparseable\\\": it exercises the\\n  NumberFormatException arm of the catch, not the IOException arm.\\n- Extract a moduleWithTempOmod test helper for the repeated\\n  module-plus-temp-omod fixture.\\n- Document in deleteLibCacheFolder why a disposed classloader keeps\\n  working on POSIX after the prune (unlink preserves its open jar\\n  handles, unlike the previous in-place overwrite that corrupted them)\\n  and that the guard refusal also returns false.\\n- Align the marker read/write warning wording.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e72a818d09b603a075ddf1040be58c9291ddb47b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-08T21:31:54+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6674: List backport releases in the minutes code @since tag (#6269)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The constant landed on 2.8.x and 2.9.x after the backports merged, so\\nthe tag now lists 2.8.8, 2.9.0 and 3.0.0 in the style of the existing\\nmulti-release tags in OpenmrsConstants. The other constants introduced\\nby TRUNK-6674 remain 3.0.0 only, since the UCUM resolution was\\ndeliberately not backported.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"4d8d419630e1ff1d46616c38573f429fd3038ff8\",\"date\":\"2026-07-08T20:47:03+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6674: Resolve drug order duration units across all known SNOMED CT and UCUM codes (#6246)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Saving a drug order whose duration units concept carries the current\\nSNOMED CT minute code 1156209001 failed with HTTP 500. SNOMED CT\\ninactivated the legacy minute code 258701004 in its 2021-07-31 release\\nand dictionaries such as CIEL now map Minutes to the active code.\\n\\nResolve duration units deterministically from all of a concept's\\nSAME-AS mappings via Duration.getDuration(Integer, Concept): SNOMED CT\\nmappings take priority and UCUM strictly fills gaps, unresolvable units\\nfail at validation instead of at save time, and getCode is deprecated\\nwith behavior unchanged. The vocabulary registries are compiled in by\\ndesign; the class Javadoc records the invariants and TRUNK-6674 records\\nthe alternatives considered.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00\",\"message\":\"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"rkorytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a6ec6555bcd71f00d07a25d2f2e8f089c4842451\",\"date\":\"2026-06-30T11:29:11+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6515: Include message broker for publishing / subscribing to external events (#6205)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit bda3963b815c36dcd768d9e515024eaff7f482a4)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":73}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UL9uUNMhYZQqpaxNRvqF9K","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
