nIntroduce a dedicated Get Alerts privilege (following the GET_* read-privilege\\nconvention) and gate both methods with it. The per-user reads (getAlerts,\\ngetAlertsByUser, getAllActiveAlerts) stay open so a user can still read their\\nown alerts. The privilege is created on startup via @AddOnStartup and is not\\nauto-granted to any role, so this does not reintroduce the leak.\\n\\nAlertReminderTask reads all alerts as its configured (possibly unprivileged)\\nscheduled-job user, so it grants itself a proxy Get Alerts privilege for that\\nread.\\n\\nUpgrade note: existing roles that relied on Manage Alerts to list alerts must\\nbe granted the new Get Alerts privilege (super users are unaffected).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Tighten cross-user alert reads on getAlert and getAlerts\\n\\ngetAllAlerts() is gated by Get Alerts, but getAlert(Integer),\\ngetAlerts(User, ...), getAlertsByUser(User) and getAllActiveAlerts(User)\\nstill let any authenticated caller read another user's alerts by passing\\nsomeone else's id/User. Guard them in the service layer: a caller may read\\ntheir own alerts, and reading another user's alerts requires the Get Alerts\\nprivilege. getAlertsByUser and getAllActiveAlerts delegate through the\\nguarded getAlerts; the self check compares userId, the same key the query\\nfilters on.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Return null from getAlert for another user's alert instead of throwing\\n\\ngetAlert(Integer) threw APIAuthenticationException when an alert existed but was addressed to another user, yet returned null for a non-existent id - letting an authenticated caller distinguish the two and probe which alert ids exist. It now returns null in both cases so the lookup cannot be used as an existence oracle. Reading one's own alert, and privileged reads via the Get Alerts privilege, are unchanged.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3f5c8a66c9f3e132036cfa362aee752a8f71b263\",\"date\":\"2026-06-08T09:34:16+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6558 Return null from getTaskByName when the task does not exist (#6163)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"JobRunrSchedulerService.getTaskByName propagated the DAO's\\nObjectRetrievalFailureException when no task matched, breaking the\\nlong-standing SchedulerService contract (the pre-JobRunr\\nTimerSchedulerServiceImpl caught the exception and returned null).\\nModules that probe for their task before registering it - e.g.\\nschedulerService.getTaskByName(NAME) == null - failed to start on any\\nfresh database.\\n\\nRestore the historical behavior: catch ObjectRetrievalFailureException,\\nlog a warning, and return null.\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"949b8a177e825320b0d04108accf38fc48751ed3\",\"date\":\"2026-06-02T20:17:10+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6643: Initial setup with MariaDB Driver does not work (#6150)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2c322bed1ac7f919fa695f68ace2f780cce9c0f4\",\"date\":\"2026-06-02T10:40:38-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6392: Improvements to the OpenMRS Logging plugin (#6104)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b3a2fa0b2d45c31065f89651f4f9801aa45354b4\",\"date\":\"2026-06-01T17:21:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria, (#6079)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria,\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* add support for searching by concept name; fix test\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* misc styling\\n\\n* change since version to 2.8.7; address feedback\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to ConceptReferenceTerm\\n\\n* switch to addUuids(String... uuids) and addConceptId(Integer... conceptIds)\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"6783feb18c2d1ede60c28af5293340cf56e0b5e8\",\"date\":\"2026-06-01T12:28:57-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6647: Add @BatchSize annotation to ConceptReferenceTerm (#6149)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"8874c97439548ef26372a9bea7a275ed9881fca6\",\"date\":\"2026-05-28T18:26:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"Use long for offset in JobRunrSchedulerService.getTasks\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"JobRunr 8.6.1 changed OffsetBasedPageRequest to take (String, Long, Integer)\\ninstead of (String, long, int); Java does not auto-widen-and-box int to Long,\\nbreaking compilation on the bump in PR #6131. Widening the local offset field\\nto long restores compatibility with both 8.5.2 and 8.6.1.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"11607283d6100942c99bcdbb6713352f62c0b53a\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18T12:09:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find … (#6088)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find descendent Locations efficiently\\n\\n* coderabbit suggestions\\n\\n* style\\n\\n* address feedback (with more efficient queries)\\n\\n* make LocationSearchCriteria take Location and LocationTag types instead of uuids\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to Location.tags to optimize location.getTags() calls\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* forward-port changes from #6089\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7590b7a4fb6c904d9cacdb0e05621ba75b6a3580\",\"date\":\"2026-04-17T17:40:15-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-